  "note": "DRAFT. The single ledger of every stat id: its layer, its principle, and its owners. Written from the 2026-10-07 design sessions (15 primaries, 3 paths x 5 principles). Weights are placeholders pending the impact census and play data; the test in tests/contracts/test_stat_ledger.gd reconciles this file against the live vocabulary and prints the distribution report. Move-for-correctness applied: absorption is TANG (soaking is containment); parry.rate is LIU; block.rate is TANG; illusion_resistance and reflect.resist.rate are LIU. Flagged, not moved: qi_affinity (L2-or-Sinh), reflect.* (Luyen stands), mental_clarity (candidate merge with sea_clarity). Rounds 2026-10-07: v1 counted exclusive owners; v2 made every channel a weighted participation of its principle's cells. A weight-cap pass (.70 then .62) moved the spread 2.77x -> 2.43x and the lesson is the round's result: caps DILUTE identity without compressing the spread, because the spread is HOME-COUNT structure. The residual (mind_soul 3.58 low, body_foundation 8.69 high) is to be closed by WIDENING the thin cells with non-combat channels, not by shaving the home weights. Non-combat block 2026-10-07: 18 new channels (crafting x5, gathering/market x4, social/fertility x3, aging/rest x3, construction/wards x2, exploration x1) homed on thin cells where the fiction allows — spread 2.43x -> 2.01x, domains combat 74 / non_combat 25 / both 10, principles 17.4/16.5/22.9/22.9/20.2. mind_soul stays the thinnest cell on purpose: the soul system is the youngest layer and its channels are the last to be authored.",
